<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    The planet is Ash'karr. Owner's NAMES ruling, design/Jawa/SCENARIO_SPEC.md (f88b2ac).

    🔑 WITH ferny.worldbuilder ACTIVE THE NAME *IS* TYPEABLE — and this patch is
    what makes the field arrive already correct. Worldbuilder's
    Page_CreateWorldParams_DoWindowContents_Patch draws a "WB_PlanetName" text
    field (:243-245), seeds it from NamerWorld on Reset
    (Page_CreateWorldParams_Reset_Patch.cs:30) and WorldGenerator_GenerateWorld_Patch
    :42-44 writes it straight to WorldInfo.info.name. Vanilla has no such field and
    generates the name from this rule pack instead.
    ⇒ Patching the rule pack covers BOTH routes, and on the Worldbuilder route it
    removes the one real hazard: the owner retyping the apostrophe and getting
    U+2019.

    ⭐ It renames throwaway dev worlds too, which is how you know it landed without
    spending the one irreversible worldgen run to find out.

    The apostrophe is U+0027 APOSTROPHE, not U+2019 RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK.
    They render alike and compare unequal. It is legal unescaped in XML text. It
    appears here and in labels only — never in a defName or a translation key.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/RulePackDef[defName="NamerWorld"]/rulePack/rulesStrings</xpath>
    <value>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>r_name->Ash'karr</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
